---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="About Us | BlueFx Markets" description="BlueFx Markets is a Windhoek forex desk for Namibian Dollar accounts." page="about">
<main id="content">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Company / About Us</p>
        <h1>A broker that speaks Namibian Dollar</h1>
        <p class="lede">BlueFx Markets is the first Namibian Best broker on this demo: a Windhoek desk, MT5 execution, and accounts that never leave NAD.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container two">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The desk</p>
          <h2>Built in Windhoek, for Namibia</h2>
          <p>Most retail forex brands ask a Namibian client to think in dollars and then convert. BlueFx starts the other way. The balance, the minimum, the bonus and the withdrawal are written in NAD. Support sits on Jan Jonker Road and answers on CAT hours, not on a night shift in another hemisphere.</p>
          <p>The product is still global. EUR/USD, gold, Wall Street and synthetic indices are all on the board. What is local is the account, the payment partner and the people who pick up support@bluefxmarkets.com.</p>
          <ul class="points">
            <li>Office: Unit 4, Maerua Mall Office Tower, Jan Jonker Road, Windhoek.</li>
            <li>Hours: Monday to Friday, 08:00–17:00 CAT. Synthetics keep trading after the desk closes.</li>
            <li>Phone: +264 61 400 2800. Email: support@bluefxmarkets.com.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-stack">
          <article><strong>2024</strong><span>Desk opened in Windhoek with NAD accounts only</span></article>
          <article><strong>2025</strong><span>MT5 and DPO Pay added for Namibian cards and EFTs</span></article>
          <article><strong>2026</strong><span>Synthetics, the iPhone app and the Android app</span></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Story</p>
        <h2>How the demo company got here</h2>
        <div class="timeline" style="margin-top:22px">
          <article>
            <h3>Windhoek, 2024</h3>
            <p>BlueFx Markets is set up to give Namibian traders a brand that prices the account in NAD. The first clients are in Windhoek, Walvis Bay and Ondangwa. The minimums are small enough for a first deposit of N$100.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Payments, 2025</h3>
            <p>DPO Pay by Network becomes the card partner. Bank Windhoek, FNB Namibia, Standard Bank Namibia and Nedbank Namibia are listed for EFTs. The cashier refuses every currency except NAD.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Markets, 2026</h3>
            <p>Synthetic indices open the week that cash FX cannot. The app ships for iPhone and Android with the NAD balance on the first screen. The account schedule grows to eleven MT5 types, including swap-free and a zero stop-out.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-grid" style="margin-top:12px">
          <article class="tool"><h3>Clear currency</h3><p>One balance currency. If a source schedule was written in rand, it is shown in NAD at one-to-one because of the peg.</p></article>
          <article class="tool"><h3>Local hours</h3><p>The desk works the Namibian business day. The calendar on the tools menu is labelled in CAT.</p></article>
          <article class="tool"><h3>Same book on the phone</h3><p>The iPhone and Android apps read the MT5 account. They do not keep a second wallet.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
